think The cadence lap is the fifth round, so the roster sang --all and two cadence choirs answered red. season_leaf_choir: 32 of 33 leaves green, one refusal -- equinox_e50 asserts LEXICON's geode row still names the five senses ending in season, and the panchanga of 20260826 replaced that word with chapter. The molt swept living prose correctly and could not see an assertion in another language holding the elder string. Booked %265, repaired, swept the tree for other living sites and found none.
think That line has now broken twice on a living sweep -- REDS %236 was the ascii-first pass turning its middots to hyphens -- so the comment beside it says so rather than leaving the next author to rediscover it.
think caravan_suite read red under the cadence roster and GREEN alone, twice, on a tree that had not moved. I could not root it, and the reason is the finding: the runner ran every guard as rishi run "$path" >/dev/null 2>&1, so a red printed one word and kept none of the guard's own. /tmp measured 1% afterwards, so REDS %239's tmpfs shape is plausible and unproven -- which is exactly the position a discarded log leaves a reader in.
think Booked %266 as an evidence repair rather than a flake fix, and said so both places. A red now keeps its guard's stdout and stderr at construction/standing-equipment-reds/<name>.txt, bounded to the last 200 lines because an unbounded log is the next thing to fill a tmpfs, cleared at every run so it never carries a stale verdict, gitignored because it records this pier's failures rather than the tree's. Proven both ways on metal: a planted refusing guard leaves its assertion message and line number, and a green run leaves no room at all.
obs Naming the flake unrooted is the honest close. Calling %266 a fix for caravan_suite would claim a cause I do not have; calling it nothing would leave the next occurrence as undiagnosable as this one. The repair is that the next red arrives with its own words.
obs The cadence tier earned its keep this lap. season_leaf_choir runs on the fifth round rather than every lap, so %265 waited exactly as long as its clock allows -- the tier working rather than the tier failing.
