think Proving the evidence capture cost two reds of my own, and both are worth writing down. First I planted a roster row pointing at a refusing witness in the LIVING roster, which left construction/standing-equipment-runs.kyri naming a guard that no longer exists -- the scan then refused with unrostered: planted_red. The control beside it already plants rosters in a git pen with STANDING_ROSTER and STANDING_CARD, which is where the proof belonged; it moved there and the card was cleaned by hand.
think Second, and structural: writing the evidence file into the working tree DURING the guard loop moves the tree under the runner's own tree_moved digest. It reads no here only because the room is gitignored; in the control's pen it turned the red into a tree_moved refusal as well. The runner already solved this exact problem for its own run card by taking tree_close BEFORE writing it, so the evidence gathers in the runner's pen during the loop and lands beside the card after the digest. The comment says which line teaches which.
think The control's new legs needed --hot, because an earlier behaviour leaves that pen's index dirty and a cold full-roster pass over a dirty index refuses before a single guard runs. That refusal is the runner working, and reading it rather than routing around it is what named the fix.
obs caravan_suite has now read GREEN alone three times against one red under the roster. The verdict stands as unrooted; three greens raise the odds it is load or a pen, and none of that is a cause. The next roster red carries its words.
loom control=standing_equipment behaviors_before=43 behaviors_after=46 new=red_keeps_both_streams,red_names_its_evidence,green_leaves_no_evidence
loom caravan_suite alone_trial_3=green roster_reds=1 alone_greens=3 root=unfound
file tools/fixtures/standing_equipment_control.sh three behaviors in the pen, gated in the control's own verdict
